SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE
The application follows a proposed three-tier architecture. 
1. Presentation Layer: Provides the homepage, destination cards, search controls, trip planner, and booking interface. 
2. Application Layer: Handles authentication, input validation, business logic, destination searches, trip operations, and booking requests. 
3. Data Layer: Stores and retrieves information about users, destinations, trips, and bookings.
 
Working Process
•	The user opens the application. 
•	The frontend displays available destinations. 
•	The user searches or filters destinations. 
•	The frontend sends a request to the backend. 
•	The backend validates the request and queries the database. 
•	The database returns matching records. 
•	The backend sends a response to the frontend. 
•	The user selects destinations and travel dates. 
•	The backend validates and stores trip or booking information. 
•	The application displays the resulting booking status.
